From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 11:58:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Lapin UX: say plainly when the disk is full at sign-in

Refs #174. A full home or state disk made sign-in fail with a wrong-password
or generic message (or none). The sign-in screen now says the disk is full
when greetd's error text says ENOSPC, when /home or /var has under 1 MiB
free, or when saving the last user or session fails with ENOSPC.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
